WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.000
So David what is the long-term plan?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.120
The long-term plan is the council's 10-year

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:13.830
plan for spending and income over
that period, it's something we do

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:18.570
every three years. So it gets refreshed
every three years and it tells our

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:24.660
community how the council intends to
develop the district in terms

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.340
of council activities over the next ten
years.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.769
It's important to realise this is

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:34.260
a draft long term plan so it's not
finalised and we do have to consult

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.180
our community about it and we welcome
that, because that community

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.160
it's their long term plan.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.200
What are the big issues
facing our district in this long-term plan?

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.840
There are a number of big issues. We've
got the continuing one of developing our

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:57.440
Regeneration areas in Kaiapoi and we used to call them red zones and a number of

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.910
projects intended for that including
work around the Kaiapoi River and

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.900
developing sports fields and passive
areas in that area.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.840
We've got the food forest already underway there,
which is a great community effort and

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:17.280
so that's to me probably the main
thing as our last few years have really been

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.200
much about earthquake recovery.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.160
Second thing is the indoor multi-sports facility

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:27.720
which is proposed for our
district, to be based in Rangiora

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:32.700
and that will provide
facilities for range of indoor sports

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:37.030
and there's been a lot of demand for that and a
lot of evidence to suggest that we are

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.840
short of that kind of space.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:43.480
Thirdly, and I think it's been very much in public's

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:48.960
mind over the last few years is our
rubbish collection facilities.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:55.880
We're looking at offering people a choice, so
that if people want three bins they can

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.400
have it, they will pay for it of course.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.200
Speaking for myself, I'll be somewhere in the middle

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.320
I'll keep my black plastic
bag because that works for me and my

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:09.440
wife but we wouldn't mind having the
green top bin for garden waste and organics.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.720
So that's there as well. We've already consulted on that.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:18.920
But finally overarching all that is
the question of rate rises and we've

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:23.540
managed to keep our rate rises fairly
low and it's also signaled to be pretty

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:31.240
low over the next 10 years and we're very aware that for many households

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.680
rates are a significant expense or
part of their total expenses for the year.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.000
Why is it important for residents to
have their say?

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.880
Because essentially it is their Long Term Plan, because it's not the council's.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.340
It's actually the Waimakariri Community's 
Long Term Plan

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.980
and it's about the directions that are being set for our community

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.300
and of course as far as
rates are concerned, it's the

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.580
community that's paying for it.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.580
How do residents make a
submission?

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.580
In a variety of ways, you can do it

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:02.180
online now, as you always see to be able
to do these days. Through our website,

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:06.860
the traditional way, through a written
submission and you can also do it by email.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:11.020
And then having done that, if you
wish to speak to the council at the

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:15.360
hearing, you're welcome to do so. 
Some people always choose to do that,

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.520
but also there will be a number of
events held throughout our district where

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.620
people can come along and ask questions
and they find out a bit more about our plans,

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:29.700
the plans we're offering to the community before we make a final decision in May.

